# Frontend

Static-first Next.js App Router. `output: 'export'`. Trailing slashes are deliberate and consistent. Generate article routes at build time.

- Server components by default. Add `"use client"` only for interaction: mobile nav, the homepage discovery control, VaultIQ stage switch, form state.
- No animation library unless a specific interaction cannot be done readably in CSS.
- No component library that sets the visual identity. Build small primitives.
- Pages compose content objects. Do not hard-code marketing copy inside layout components.
- Images must work on static export. Decorative images need empty alt text. Portraits need real alternative text once photography exists.
- One `h1` per page. Do not skip heading levels.

```tsx
// Wrong: copy trapped in the component
export function Hero() {
  return <h1>Revolutionizing the digital landscape</h1>;
}

// Right: copy from typed content
export function Hero({ hero }: { hero: HomeContent["hero"] }) {
  return <h1>{hero.headline}</h1>;
}
```

Target routes and file roles are in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
